{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1410334-violent-solves-everything-your-character-s-movelist","id":1410334,"title":"Violent solves EVERYTHING: Your character's Movelist","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-25T10:59:00-07:00","id":1410334,"title":"Violent solves EVERYTHING: Your character's Movelist","content":"<div align=\"center\"><img src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/498704231407288320/747891850815471736/image0.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> <br /> <br /> So choosing charms for me is super easy, just pick what looks cool! But actually making a distinctive fighting style and tactic is not so easy, so I thought about making them into fighting game's characters first, visualizing a combo string is much easier than some paragraph stunt essay. You guys can join in if think it's interesting, reading about other people's special moves would be quite fun ~( ^o^)~<br /> <br /> I'm thinking that each character will have a Unique trait that modifies their normal mechanic which amplifies with their playstyle, something like wall-jump, or powering-up for charge bar,...etc. And there are Light/Medium/Heavy attacks (A/B/C respectively), special move using the Heavy button will be an EX move which cost 25% charge bar. Holding D while at 99/100 charge bar will let the character enter a stage call Anima Release/Bonfire Release which lets them perform special move which is calls.....August Arts I guess? I can't think of a good Exalted name for that kind of move, since Limit Break is already taken in the book. And the charge bar can be called the Mote Pool, obviously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","user":"Jen","date":". 08-25-2020, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T10:59:52-07:00","id":1410335,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Theodotus, the Noon Witch</span></b></span><br /> <br /> A magician who harasses the opponent from afar with sorcery, he can adjust his playstyles easily between pure zoning, rushdown, or mid-space control. A character who can easily snowball into victory but will lose a lot of his momentum if forced into the defense position due to his lack of good reversal and get-off-me options.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Strength</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><ul><li>Obnoxious normals and specials that can hit at odd angles and allowing knockdown at anywhere on the screen.</li> <li>Diverse choices of projectiles allow him to have incredible space control and mixup options.</li> <li>Suffocating and ambiguous pressure that is almost inescapable thanks to orbs that can automatically or manually detonate.</li> <li>Unique trait gives him hard-to-predict air movement to aid in his already terrifying pressure.</li> <li>Fast dash to quickly close the distance for setup on a knockdown opponent.</li> <li>Extremely potent August Art with low damage but seals the opponent's Essence pool, cutting off many options for getting out of pressure.</li> </ul></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Weakness</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><ul><li>Required holding buttons for the harder setups.</li> <li>Some projectiles would disappear when he's hit.</li> <li>Vulnerable to aggressive rushdown if he hasn't set up any projectiles on the screen yet.</li> <li>Normal attacks have lengthy startup which makes it hard to peel off pressure when he's in melee range.</li> <li>Slow and floaty jump means jumping out of pressure is much harder than other characters.</li> <li>Become a meatbag if cornered and has no meter since only the Ex ver of his reversal has plus frame on block.</li> </ul></td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <u><b><img src=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/498704231407288320/747479224276877322/image0.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Unique Traits:</span></b></u><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Fly Like a Fish, Swim Like a Bird - (j)DD </span></b><br /> The first flying fish in Creation? Probably not. Allowing Theo to hover and glides on the air in any directions up to 4 seconds. Entering flight will reset his airdash if you have already used it, combined with his ability to cancel any special moves into flight allows applying strong pressure on a wakeup opponent.<br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Special Moves:</span></b></u><br /> <br /> <b>DEATH RAY! Just kiddin'! - 236ABC</b><br /> Conjure an obsidian butterfly that goes in a straight line, can hold to create more butterflies in an arc which stay in place as long as the button is held, A version will fly off instantly while B version has a slight delay, C version fires out one butterfly that explodes which gives massive plus frame on block. The normal version will be your main zoning tool due to its height when fully charge, while the EX butterfly can help extend a combo string and punish some moves due to its fast speed.<br /> <br /> <b>It's a blessing ball, you should touch it! - 214ABC</b><br /> Summoning the Ball right in front of Theo. You can have up to three balls on the screen for each button, can be charged up which gives them even more plus frame and become air-unblockable. Being forced to block one would mean an inescapable pressure string where he can setup even more projectiles.<br /> <br /> <b>I'm already engaged! - (j)236236ABC</b><br /> Create an essence field around you, A/B version causes unrecoverable knockdown and wallslam respectively while the EX version causes both. Can be used as a combo-ender for pressure or reset the game to neutral. The AB version on the ground has invul frame but can be easily punished if blocked, while the aerial version doesn't but is neutral and can be used in mixup to force knockdown on the opponent.<br /> <br /> <b>It's the Arrow of LOOOOOVE - 22ABC</b><br /> Lob an orb into the air that will rain down arrows when the button is released, A version has more arrows on a narrow area while B version is the opposite, blocking both versions can easily Guard Break an opponent due to the high number of hits.<br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">August Arts:</span></b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Sun God's Immeasurable Banquet/Great Sun Devouring All Under Heaven - 41236C during Anima Release/Bonfire Release</b><br /> Surprisingly no vore is involved. A grab that depletes 50% of the opponent Mote Pool and seals it for 5 seconds, increases to 100% and 10s for the Bonfire Release version. Will cause unrecoverable knockdown which allow Theo to do his usual thing. Require Theo to ignite his anima so the enemy will see this coming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T08:03:46-07:00","id":1410516,"title":"","content":"I like this idea a lot.<br /> <br /> I've been using Musou games as a way to find a character's stunt 'voice' myself. One Piece, Pirate Warriors 4, for instance; while the actual One Piece story has gotten so convoluted and difficult to follow with way too many characters, I find the Musou game to be really good for having a series of moves that look good to watch and can help me go 'oh, yeah, this is how that should look'.<br /> <br /> I'll have to think about this and come up with something later, because it's a really interesting idea and I want to do it right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T12:11:33-07:00","id":1411013,"title":"","content":"Okay, my power went out for a few days but I managed to get this put out. I play DBFZ, so I made a character based on DBFZ's style of play. <br /> <br /> <b><u>Soheil Al'Fard, Endings Caste Sidereal</u></b><br /> <br /> <div align=\"left\"> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 468px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Strengths</span></span></div></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Weaknesses</span></span></div></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\"><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Incredible damage, with a light that scales like a Medium and a Medium that scales like a heavy</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Great Frame data means he can punish slow start ups.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Level 1 and Level 3 Meterburn Super give tremendous flexibility on damage output.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Special moves give mobility and mix-up.</span></span></li> </ul></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\"><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Incredible meter hog with poor assists; he is an anchor who requires a team be built around him</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">No projectile game outside of borrowed specials, meaning his neutral game is dependent on his own special moves to get in close</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Incredibly fragile; his defense relies entirely on reading the opponent to get out of pressure</span></span></li> </ul></td> </tr> </table></div> </div> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Important Normals;</span></span></b></u><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>2H;</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Soheil\u2019s 2H is a huge backflipping kick. It has a faster then average startup, and he is upper body invincible during it. However, it misses crouchers and low hits will hit him.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>6L;</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> A jumping kick, this button has long reach and hits overhead, making it great as a mix-up.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>22S: Manusya;</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Soheil bends down then super jumps up with a blast of air. If the opponent is hit by this, they are knocked into the air with Soheil. Great for continuing combos, but has a slower start up then normal super jumping, making timing it against super dashes incredibly tricky, but it scales very well meaning its risky but rewarding.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>j.2L;</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> a two hit kick, his best option for cross up after jumping forward, due to how fast it comes out</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>j.3H; Asura;</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> A driving punch that carries to the wall for a Smash, it has tremendous corner carry but scales heavily once used</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>S while superdashing; Deva;</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> a disjoint that phases Soheil, removing him from hitting or being hit while he dashes. The invulnerable period is short, but if he would hit the target while invulnerable, he will super dash through them to the other side, then stop, which can allow him insane mixup combos. He can still be 2H'd or dp'd in between when he gets through the opponent and when he stops moving, and it will autocorrect if timed properly, meaning cautious play will punish Soheil for a risky maneuver. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>4S; Preta;</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> A single finger poke with average range. It beats beams on hit, protecting him from getting hit by them, but is a melee range attack. If Vanish is used, Soheil will have time to block the sideswitch if he reacts. In combos, it can only be used once but provides massive hitstun to continue the combo.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Specials;</span></span></b></u><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>236 L/M/H: Tiryag:</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Soheil vanishes. L jumps backwards then vanishes, M leaps up and vanishes, H instantly vanishes. Inputting a new button causes a follow up, holding or not pressing will follow up with the same button. Air Okay.</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>L:</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u> Wolf:</u> Soheil appears in front of the target with a low kick</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>M:</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u> Eagle:</u> Soheil appears above and does a dropping knee. Does not sideswitch when chained from Light or Medium, does from Heavy. In Air, will cause sliding knockdown </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>H:</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u> Leopard:</u> Soheil strikes with both hands from behind the opponent. Causes a wall bounce on hit if Smash hasn't been used.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>214 L/M/H: Naraka</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Soheil takes a stance that makes him invulnerable for 1 hit while it is active. He then launches an extremely short range command grab. If the invulnerability is triggered, the opponent will get hit by the Command Grab no matter what, turning it into a Counter. The Light version has fast start up but multiple hits will break the armor, and causes a crumple state on hit. The medium version will have super armor for hits past the first but becomes invulnerable slower. The heavy version starts instantly and will cancel any attacks past the one that triggered the invuln.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>236S: I can do that, too.:</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Soheil copies the 236S of the first character on his team. On the second activation, he uses the other character's. He alternates consistently, and the game keeps track of which is next through swaps. If a partner.is knocked out, he still continues to use the move.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>214S; I've already learned that.:</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Soheil copies the 214S of an enemy character. It starts at the 1st position then cycles through from there. Similarly to 236S, he will still use the moves of characters that have been defeated.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Super moves</u></span></span></b></u><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>236L+M (ground only); Dragon's Claw:</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Soheil executes a command grab on his opponent, taking a step forward and swiping downwards to catch aerial foes as well. On contact, he slams them into the ground and causes an explosion of purple flames, dealing damage. The damage is low for a Super, but it offers great Oki, as Soheil will finish the move standing directly next to his opponent for jump in.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>236L+M (Air Only); Piercing Heron:</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Soheil drops directly down and strikes his opponent with a piercing hand. The damage is strong for a Super, but difficult to land unless the opponent is in the corner. This is the DHC Super for Soheil. Like Dragon's Claw, it has good Oki as it deposits Soheil directly in front of his opponent.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>236 H+S; Samsara (Air Ok);</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Soheil takes a stance and then unleashes a wave of air pressure at his opponent. This functions as a screen length Super that can be jumped over. The damage is increased if the opponent is close enough that his extending fists strike the opponent</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>H+S; Emperor Elephant:</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> by holding down the button, expend an extra level of Meter for Soheil to dash past the opponent and strike them rapidly, causing a sideswitch.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>214 L+M or H+S; I still haven't reached my potential (Air Ok);</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Cinematic Level 3. Soheil kicks the opponent up into the air, then pummels them with strikes before knocking them back to the ground. Has poor Oki but good damage, leaving Soheil with limited ways to re-engage on wake-up outside of 236LMH mixups or jumping 6L. </span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>L+M or H+S: Burning King Cobra;</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Soheil catches the opponent right before they land with a hammering double blow with his hands in the shape of a snake's biting mouth, causing an explosion of purple fire. This move does extreme damage, but Soheil can't effectively apply pressure after it, as he has a recovery period while the opponent wakes up, essentially resetting the game to neutral.</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Assists</u></span></span></b></u><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Assist A; Preta;</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Soheil appears in front of the ally and uses Preta. Like his own move, it will defeat projectiles, allowing the ally to use their own beam to convert, or do significant hitstun if blocked during a block string. Likely his best assist, but primarily good for defense in neutral, as timing it to block a beam can grant a chance to start a beam into vanish for the ally.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Assist B; I can do that, too.;</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Soheil does the next 236S in his rotation.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Assist C; Manusya</u></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">; Soheil does his Manusya move, then, if it hits, appears above the opponent and knocks them back towards the ground.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}